    "question": {
      "text": "For two matrices $A$ and $B$, if $AB=A$ and $BA=B$, then which of the following statements is/are correct?\nI. $A$ is an idempotent matrix.\nII. $B$ is an idempotent matrix.",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "I only"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "II only"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "Both I and II"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "Neither I nor II"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "C",
      "correctText": "Both I and II",
      "explanation": "Given $AB=A$ and $BA=B$. From $BA=B$, $A(BA)=AB$, hence $(AB)A=A$, giving $A^2=A$. Thus $A$ is an idempotent matrix. From $AB=A$, $B(AB)=BA$, hence $(BA)B=B$, giving $B^2=B$. Thus $B$ is an idempotent matrix. Hence both I and II are correct. Choice (C).",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    "classification": {
      "subject": "Engineering Mathematics",
      "topic": "Linear Algebra",
      "subtopic": "Matrices and determinants",
