      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "C",
      "correctText": "an involutory matrix",
      "explanation": "Given $A$ is non-singular and $A^3=A$. Thus $AA^2=A$. Multiplying by $A^{-1}$ gives $A^2=I$. Hence $A$ must be an involutory matrix. Choice (C).",
