      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "B",
      "correctText": "$2$",
      "explanation": "Given matrix is $P$. Applying $R_2\\to R_2-2R_1$, $R_3\\to R_3-4R_1$ and $R_4\\to R_4-3R_1$, followed by row reduction, gives a row echelon form with two non-zero rows. Hence the rank of $P$ is 2. Choice (B).",
