    "question": {
      "text": "If $A$ is a $3\\times3$ matrix with the characteristic equation $\\lambda^3-5\\lambda^2+2\\lambda-3=0$, then $3A^9-15A^8+6A^7-11A^6+10A^5-4A^4+10A^3-20A^2+8A-9I$ is equal to _______.",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$\\begin{bmatrix}1&0&0\\\\0&1&0\\\\0&0&1\\end{bmatrix}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$\\begin{bmatrix}2&0&0\\\\0&2&0\\\\0&0&2\\end{bmatrix}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$\\begin{bmatrix}3&0&0\\\\0&3&0\\\\0&0&3\\end{bmatrix}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$\\begin{bmatrix}4&0&0\\\\0&4&0\\\\0&0&4\\end{bmatrix}$"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "C",
      "correctText": "$\\begin{bmatrix}3&0&0\\\\0&3&0\\\\0&0&3\\end{bmatrix}$",
      "explanation": "By Cayley-Hamilton theorem, $A^3-5A^2+2A-3I=0$. Rewriting the given expression using this relation reduces it to $3I$. Hence the required matrix is $3I=\\begin{bmatrix}3&0&0\\\\0&3&0\\\\0&0&3\\end{bmatrix}$. Choice (C).",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
